# npm 12 stopped running dependency lifecycle scripts by default: a package's
# postinstall only runs if the package is named in `allowScripts`.
#
# @anthropic-ai/claude-code ships a ~500-byte placeholder at bin/claude.exe and
# relies on its postinstall (`node install.cjs`) to hardlink the ~250MB
# platform-native binary over it. With the postinstall blocked the placeholder
# survives, and every `claude` invocation dies with:
#
#     Error: claude native binary not installed.
#
# npm still exits 0 and only mentions it in a `warn install-scripts` line, so
# the install looks like it worked.
#
# This matters far beyond the first install: Claude Code's auto-updater runs
# `npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code@<version>` on its own schedule.
# Without this file, every release it picks up silently reverts a working
# install back to the placeholder -- which shows up as "the claude binary
# disappeared again after I restarted", with nothing having changed locally.
#
# @openai/codex has no install scripts and needs no entry here.
allow-scripts=@anthropic-ai/claude-code
